AWS S3 Setup for Snowflake – Step-by-Step Guide
Step 1: Create an AWS Account
Go to the AWS website.
Click Create an AWS Account.
Enter the following details:
Email Address
Password
AWS Account Name
Verify your email address.
Add your payment method.
Complete phone verification.
Select the Free Tier plan.
Sign in to the AWS Management Console.
Step 2: Create an S3 Bucket
In the AWS Console, search for S3.
Click S3.
Click Create bucket.

Enter the following information:

Bucket Name:
snowflake-s3-new-bucket4

Leave all other settings as default.

Click Create bucket.

Step 3: Upload Files to the Bucket
Open the bucket you created.
Click Upload.
Click Add files.
Select your files.

Example:

emp.csv
dept.csv
Click Upload.
Step 4: Create an IAM User
Search for IAM in the AWS Console.
Open IAM.
Select Users from the left menu.
Click Create user.

Example:

User Name:
snowflake_new_user

Click Next.

Step 5: Assign Permissions

Choose:

Attach policies directly

Search for:

AmazonS3FullAccess

Select the policy.

Click:

Next

Finally, click:

Create user
Step 6: Generate Access Keys
Open the IAM user you created.
Go to the Security credentials tab.
Scroll down to Access keys.
Click Create access key.
Select:
Command Line Interface (CLI)
Click Next.
Click Create access key.

You will receive:

Access Key ID

Secret Access Key

Important: Download the CSV file or copy both keys immediately. The Secret Access Key is displayed only once.




SNOWFLAKE SETUP
---------------

STEP 1;CREATE TABLE

CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE DEPT
(
    DEPTNO NUMBER,
    DNAME STRING,
    LOC STRING
);

select * from dept;(NO ROWS)

STEP 2 
-------

CREATE FILE FORMAT;

CREATE OR REPLACE FILE FORMAT MY_DEPT_FORMAT
TYPE = CSV
SKIP_HEADER = 1;



STEP 3
------

CREATE STAGE
AND PROVIDE ACCESS KEY.

CREATE OR REPLACE STAGE MY_S3_STAGE
URL='s3://snowflake-s3newbucket4'
CREDENTIALS=(
AWS_KEY_ID='**************',
AWS_SECRET_KEY='******************************');


LIST @MY_S3_STAGE;


STEP 5
------

CREATE PIPE TO LOAD THE DATA FROM STAGE TO SNOWFLAKE TABLE.


CREATE OR REPLACE PIPE DEPT_PIPE
AS
COPY INTO DEPT
FROM @MY_S3_STAGE
FILE_FORMAT = (FORMAT_NAME='MY_DEPT_FORMAT');




STEP 6
------
MANUAL REFRESH
-----------------

ALTER PIPE DEPT_PIPE REFRESH;

select * froM EMP;




FOR AUTO REFRESH:
-----------------

STEP 1; 
--------
CREATE ANY TABLE
----------------

CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE EMP
(
EMPNO NUMBER,
ENAME STRING,
JOB STRING,
MGR NUMBER,
HIREDATE DATE,
SAL NUMBER,
COMM NUMBER,
DEPTNO NUMBER
);


select * from emp;

STEP 2:
-------
CREATE PIPE FOR EMP;


CREATE OR REPLACE PIPE EMP_PIPE
AS
COPY INTO EMP
FROM @MY_S3_STAGE
FILE_FORMAT = (FORMAT_NAME = 'MY_CSV_FORMAT');



STEP 3;
-------


select * from emp;(NO ROWS)

WHY BECAUS OUR IN S3 BUCKET WE NEED TO UPLOAD EMP.CSV;

NOW UPLOAD EMP.CSV IN AWS S3 BUCKET.

STEP 4;
-------

CREATE TASK FOR AUTO REFRESH.
------------------------------


CREATE OR REPLACE TASK REFRESH_PIPE_TASK
WAREHOUSE = MYWH
SCHEDULE = '1 MINUTE'
AS
ALTER PIPE EMP_PIPE REFRESH;


STEP 5;
-------
RESUME THE TASK.

ALTER TASK REFRESH_PIPE_TASK RESUME;


FOR SUSPEND
-------------

ALTER TASK REFRESH_PIPE_TASK suspend;


select * from emp;(ROWS DISPLAYED) WITHIN 1 MIN.

